<DocsLayout title="Exchange RBAC and sender authorization" description="Understand how RelayBridge uses Exchange Application RBAC to scope SMTP authorization to one selected Exchange Online sender mailbox." section="Microsoft 365">
  <section>
    <h2>Identity and authorization are separate</h2>
    <p>The certificate-backed Entra application proves which software requests a Microsoft token. Exchange Application RBAC determines what that application may do. RelayBridge uses sender-scoped RBAC rather than a broad Entra mail permission.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Objects created or verified by setup</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>the Exchange service-principal reference for the customer-owned Entra application;</li>
      <li>a RelayBridge-marked distribution group containing only the selected sender mailbox;</li>
      <li>a management scope whose recipient filter is tied to that group; and</li>
      <li>exactly one scoped <code>Application SMTP.SendAsApp</code> assignment for the application.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Setup verifies that the selected mailbox is in scope and that conflicting or extra grants are absent. Unexpected broadening fails validation instead of being silently accepted.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Sender boundary during delivery</h2>
    <p>The active sender must be a real Exchange Online mailbox. Every queued envelope sender must match that active sender, and every local device also has an exact sender allowlist.</p>
    <div class="docs-callout-security docs-callout">
      <strong>Authorize the SMTP envelope, not the display header</strong>
      <p>Do not rely on the message-header <code>From</code> value or display name as the authorization boundary. RelayBridge evaluates the SMTP envelope sender before durable acceptance and uses that queued envelope sender for Exchange delivery.</p>
    </div>
    <p>RelayBridge does not request mailbox-reading access. Tenant-side edits to the sender group, management scope, service-principal reference, or role assignment can invalidate prior evidence and require repair or verification.</p>
  </section>

